140 DROP TABLES Tmp_Txn, Tmp_Risk;	Removes the temporary tables. If they stayed, both would link through transaction_id and inflate your counts.

Extra lines in your newest version:

account_id as %account_key, customer_id as %customer_key and branch_id as %branch_key do the same job as %txn_key. They are hidden links to the dimension tables.
The long nested If ... as risk_status checks from the strictest group down. It gives ‘Fraud-suspected’ if there’s a High flag and at least 2 flags, otherwise ‘High-risk’ if there’s a High flag, otherwise ‘Flagged (Low/Medium)’ if there’s any flag, and otherwise ‘Clean’. Order matters: the first condition that is true wins.
